{{- /*
The account-wide half of a Claude Code enrolment, written by `faramir init`: a
deny-only copy of the PreToolUse hook, and the deny rules that refuse a path to
its file tools.

Both in a home rather than a tree. The wrapper, the redactor and the binary the
hook execs are installed for the account, so nothing about routing needs a tree,
and an operator's declared paths are the host's rather than any project's. A
tree carries the prose and the routing copy of this hook, in
.claude/settings.local.json, which `faramir enrol` writes.

Deny-only, and that is the whole of the difference from the tree's. A rewrite
has to be approved to run, and the allow that approves it approves every command
the list does not name; Claude Code refuses the permission rule that would
approve the rewrite instead, saying "'source' evaluates arguments as shell code".
So routing costs a permission here and nowhere else, and an operator takes that
trade per tree. What this one does is refuse what the list names, wherever the
agent is working, and say nothing about anything else: a silent answer leaves
the host's own permission flow as it was.

The matcher is "*" rather than "Bash". An empty reply is a call left alone, so
answering for a tool that runs nothing costs nothing, and matching every tool is
what puts the file tools in front of the deny list at all.

That matters because the rules below and the hook are one enforcement each
rather than one enforcement written twice. Claude Code applies a deny rule in
every permission mode, bypassPermissions included, and the hook runs in every
mode too, but a rule can be edited out of this file and a hook can be turned
off wholesale with disableAllHooks. Each covers the other's absence.

GENERATED. The paths come from internal/install/protectedpaths.go, written
once and rendered into each agent's own spelling; nothing here is a path of its
own. Add one there.

Read and Edit rules only: Claude Code matches file permission checks against
Edit(path), which covers every file-editing tool, and a Write(path) rule matches
nothing.

Two leading slashes on every path. One anchors the pattern at this file rather
than at the filesystem root, so Read(/home/op/.age) here asks about
~/.claude/home/op/.age and refuses nothing at all.

Read and Edit take the same list. A value the agent cannot read is one it can
still destroy, and an age key replaced is every managed file unreadable
retroactively.
*/ -}}
{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "{{.BinDir}}/faramir guard --deny-only",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
{{ jsonLines "      " (claudeRules .Layout) }}
    ]
  }
}
